Set up the array for storing the pitch sequence.
~~~
'vals var @Free !vals #9 allot #8 @vals store

#0 #5 #7 #10 #12 #10 #7 #5
#8 [
@vals
#7 I n:sub
a:store
] indexed-times

~~~
Set up a context for creating a patch. Make sure that
the address of this context is set to cursor 0.
~~~
son:ctx-create #0 son:cur son:go
~~~
Convert a clock signal into a
trigger signal via metro.
~~~
#125 #4 n:mul const clock metro
~~~
Create an array of 8 8-bit (2^3) values, packed in a
single word: len.wrdsz.
~~~
#3 #8 #4 shift-left or son:array-create
~~~
Retrieve the array address (pop, rwget), and populate
with sequence values in the array stack.
~~~
son:pop son:rw-get
#8 [ dup @vals I a:fetch #60 n:add I son:array-write ] indexed-times
~~~
Create an array iterator, followed by the sequencer
~~~
son:iter seq #0.001 constf smoother
~~~
The rest of the patch
~~~
mtof saw #200 const lpf #0.500 constf mul sink
#0 setw topen
#0 last-ugen son:rw-get bind
#11 render
#0 setw tclose
son:ctx-destroy
bye
~~~
